1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,314
The better question arrived over dinner on the eighth of August.

2
00:00:03,314 --> 00:00:21,577
“Our deadline is overdue,” Maya said, “and the renewal is not the priority.” A delegation from the council had asked for a description of how the figures were used, and the statistical office had sent back something that was not a description at all.

3
00:00:21,577 --> 00:00:31,021
The little office, the court date, and the great unfinished film were all in the same report for the first time.

4
00:00:31,021 --> 00:00:36,860
The false assumption was simple: that a punctual team is a keen team.

5
00:00:36,860 --> 00:00:41,435
“We recommend a different matter for today,” Lin said.

6
00:00:41,435 --> 00:00:57,548
“Yesterday we sewed the same sleeve twice.” The telescope, the chef, and the commodity trader in the same lift all had a theory about the following month, and the march of dates was the thrust of the whole argument.

7
00:00:57,548 --> 00:01:07,832
The trademark of the film was its authenticity, and authenticity was indicative of something else: they had not foreseen the extra work.

8
00:01:07,832 --> 00:01:18,706
A buckle, a supplementary line, and the twelfth paragraph had been added after the launch, and the consequent delay was now in the report.

9
00:01:18,706 --> 00:01:25,610
A day after the following one, they would go back and count the cost again.

10
00:01:25,610 --> 00:01:28,685
The subsequent meeting was short.

11
00:01:28,685 --> 00:01:40,423
They concluded that the push for control had cost them the enjoyment of the work, and that the desirability of a fast release was a matter of the head, not of the house.

12
00:01:40,423 --> 00:01:45,778
“Immediately” became “by the ninth”, and “we must” became “we will”.

13
00:01:45,778 --> 00:01:53,722
The family name on the office door, for the moment, meant more to them than the deadline.

14
00:01:53,722 --> 00:01:57,876
The little business went on with its small tasks.

15
00:01:57,876 --> 00:02:02,376
“A flock of them is not a plan,” Maya said.

16
00:02:02,376 --> 00:02:18,044
“Something has to move, or nothing will.” She was right, and she was also tired; the better question, in the end, was not when the film would be finished but who would be blamed if it were not.

17
00:02:18,044 --> 00:02:24,799
It was likely that nobody would thank them, and likely that the following month would be worse.

18
00:02:24,799 --> 00:02:34,478
They were, in a word, tired, and the tiredness was the extra cost that nobody had described.
